{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G6xVPqqELsJHU49mB3VUnS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Release runbook\n2\t\n3\t`.github/workflows/version.yml` tags every first-parent merge to `main` as `vX.Y.Z` and creates a notes-only release. This runbook covers setup and recovery. Names come from the workflow.\n4\t\n5\t## Seed tag\n6\t\n7\tAn admin creates the annotated seed tag once, on a commit on `main`:\n8\t\n9\t```\n10\tgit tag -a v0.1.0 <sha> -m v0.1.0\n11\tgit push origin refs/tags/v0.1.0\n12\t```\n13\t\n14\tUntil it exists a dry run plans nothing and a live run fails.\n15\t\n16\t## Settings checklist\n17\t\n18\t- Repository variables: `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (ard's App login, `<slug>[bot]`), `ARD_VERSIONING` (`on` for live), `RELEASE_APP_ID`, `RELEASE_BOT_NAME`, `RELEASE_BOT_EMAIL`.\n19\t- A `release` environment holding the secret `RELEASE_APP_PRIVATE_KEY`. The release App needs contents: write only, and must not be ard's App.\n20\t\n21\t## Homebrew release (release.yml)\n22\t\n23\t`.github/workflows/release.yml` runs on each `v*` tag `version.yml` pushes (and on `workflow_dispatch` with a `tag`). It builds the four archives with GoReleaser (`.goreleaser.yaml`), uploads them and `checksums.txt` to the tag's existing release, and updates `Casks/ard.rb` in `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap`.\n24\t\n25\t- It does nothing until `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on` **and** the `release` environment holds the secret `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`. Without the token it logs a notice and stops.\n26\t- `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`: a fine-grained token (or a second App's token) with **contents: read and write on `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap` only**. Store it only in the `release` environment.\n27\t- Create `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap` (public, with a `Casks/` directory) and protect its `main`.\n28\t- On a tag push only the newest `v*` tag is released, so a backfill of many tags publishes once. To build an older tag: `gh workflow run release.yml -R albertcbrown/ard -f tag=vX.Y.Z`.\n29\t- One release runs at a time (`concurrency: release`, never cancelled).\n30\t- Check locally first: `make release-check` (snapshot, publishes nothing).\n31\t\n32\t## Dry run to live\n33\t\n34\tEvery run is a dry run until `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on`. Check the plan in a dry run's step summary, then set the variable. `workflow_dispatch` is a dry run unless `dry_run` is false; `max_tags` (default 20) caps the tags one run creates, so raise it after reading the plan when a backlog is larger.\n35\t\n36\t## Bumps and the module path\n37\t\n38\tLabel a PR `semver:minor` or `semver:major`; with neither it is a patch, and with both major wins. Go requires a `/vN` module path for N >= 2. A `semver:major` that would reach v2 stops the run (exit 2) until `go.mod` says `module .../v2`; relabel the PR or change `go.mod`, then rerun.\n39\t\n40\t## Recovery\n41\t\n42\t- A failed run stops at the first failure. Rerun it: the plan is rebuilt from the tags that exist, and a tag without a release gets a release-only backfill row.\n43\t- Never delete or move a tag. If a tag is wrong, fix forward with the next version.\n44\t- `ard version` prints the tag after `make build` on a tagged commit, and after `go install github.com/albertcbrown/ard/cmd/ard@vX.Y.Z`.\n45\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45379bcf-1105-43f4-9d7c-90b4cdbd049a","uuid":"36156d1a-49ef-4962-b827-20a778f7182e","timestamp":"2026-11-25T08:50:17.366Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/work/docs/runbooks/release.md","content":"# Release runbook\n\n`.github/workflows/version.yml` tags every first-parent merge to `main` as `vX.Y.Z` and creates a notes-only release. This runbook covers setup and recovery. Names come from the workflow.\n\n## Seed tag\n\nAn admin creates the annotated seed tag once, on a commit on `main`:\n\n```\ngit tag -a v0.1.0 <sha> -m v0.1.0\ngit push origin refs/tags/v0.1.0\n```\n\nUntil it exists a dry run plans nothing and a live run fails.\n\n## Settings checklist\n\n- Repository variables: `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (ard's App login, `<slug>[bot]`), `ARD_VERSIONING` (`on` for live), `RELEASE_APP_ID`, `RELEASE_BOT_NAME`, `RELEASE_BOT_EMAIL`.\n- A `release` environment holding the secret `RELEASE_APP_PRIVATE_KEY`. The release App needs contents: write only, and must not be ard's App.\n\n## Homebrew release (release.yml)\n\n`.github/workflows/release.yml` runs on each `v*` tag `version.yml` pushes (and on `workflow_dispatch` with a `tag`). It builds the four archives with GoReleaser (`.goreleaser.yaml`), uploads them and `checksums.txt` to the tag's existing release, and updates `Casks/ard.rb` in `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap`.\n\n- It does nothing until `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on` **and** the `release` environment holds the secret `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`. Without the token it logs a notice and stops.\n- `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`: a fine-grained token (or a second App's token) with **contents: read and write on `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap` only**. Store it only in the `release` environment.\n- Create `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap` (public, with a `Casks/` directory) and protect its `main`.\n- On a tag push only the newest `v*` tag is released, so a backfill of many tags publishes once. To build an older tag: `gh workflow run release.yml -R albertcbrown/ard -f tag=vX.Y.Z`.\n- One release runs at a time (`concurrency: release`, never cancelled).\n- Check locally first: `make release-check` (snapshot, publishes nothing).\n\n## Dry run to live\n\nEvery run is a dry run until `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on`. Check the plan in a dry run's step summary, then set the variable. `workflow_dispatch` is a dry run unless `dry_run` is false; `max_tags` (default 20) caps the tags one run creates, so raise it after reading the plan when a backlog is larger.\n\n## Bumps and the module path\n\nLabel a PR `semver:minor` or `semver:major`; with neither it is a patch, and with both major wins. Go requires a `/vN` module path for N >= 2. A `semver:major` that would reach v2 stops the run (exit 2) until `go.mod` says `module .../v2`; relabel the PR or change `go.mod`, then rerun.\n\n## Recovery\n\n- A failed run stops at the first failure. Rerun it: the plan is rebuilt from the tags that exist, and a tag without a release gets a release-only backfill row.\n- Never delete or move a tag. If a tag is wrong, fix forward with the next version.\n- `ard version` prints the tag after `make build` on a tagged commit, and after `go install github.com/albertcbrown/ard/cmd/ard@vX.Y.Z`.\n","numLines":45,"startLine":1,"totalLines":45}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01G6xVPqqELsJHU49mB3VUnS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
