{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018fn39gKBj6trWmF8WhMwbQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ard — automated repository development\n2\t\n3\tard makes a GitHub repository maintain itself. Scanners file deduplicated issues, triage agents turn each issue into a plan, a worker agent implements it on a branch, reviewer agents critique the PR, and a merger lands it once every review passes.\n4\t\n5\t**Documentation:** <https://albertcbrown.github.io/ard/> (sources in [docs/site](docs/site)).\n6\t\n7\t> **Status:** under active development. The design lives in [docs/proposal.md](docs/proposal.md), and the work is tracked as [GitHub issues](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues) grouped into phase milestones.\n8\t\n9\t## How it works\n10\t\n11\tOne rule holds the system together: **a deterministic controller owns every GitHub and git side effect; agents only read and write files in a worktree.**\n12\t\n13\tOne `ard` process per repository runs six loops that share a small pool of job slots (default 3):\n14\t\n15\t| Loop | Every | What it does |\n16\t| --- | --- | --- |\n17\t| Scanners | 4 h | Find problems (CVEs, outdated components, lint, docs, missing tests…), file or update issues, close what is fixed |\n18\t| Triage | 15 min | Role agents (lead, PM, architect, designer, doc planner, engineer) turn an issue into `plan.md` |\n19\t| Workers | 5 min | Implement the plan on `worker/<role>-<issue#>-<slug>`, run tests, open a draft PR |\n20\t| Reviewers | 5 min | Role agents (security, license, eng, PM) review the PR and request fixes |\n21\t| Merger | 5 min | Squash-merge PRs whose reviews all passed and whose checks are green |\n22\t| Reaper | 1 min | Mark dead or overdue jobs `ard:executor:failed`, keep their evidence 24 h |\n23\t\n24\tGitHub labels prefixed `ard:` are the queue and the state machine. `.ard/<issue#>/` in the target repository holds each issue's plan, per-role summaries and full agent logs.\n25\t\n26\t## Configuration by convention\n27\t\n28\tA target repository opts in with an `.ard/` directory. A role exists because its directory exists:\n29\t\n30\t```\n31\t.ard/\n32\t├── config.yaml          # global settings and overrides only\n33\t├── scanners/<name>/     # scan (executable) or prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n34\t├── triage/<name>/       # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n35\t├── workers/<name>/      # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n36\t├── reviewers/<name>/    # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n37\t└── <issue#>/            # per-issue output and logs, written only by ard\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\tSee [Configuration](docs/proposal.md#configuration) in the proposal for the full schema and defaults.\n41\t\n42\t## Development\n43\t\n44\tRequires Go (see `go.mod`).\n45\t\n46\t```bash\n47\tmake build   # builds bin/ard\n48\tmake test    # go test ./...\n49\tmake lint    # go vet and a gofmt check\n50\t```\n51\t\n52\tContributor and agent guidance is in [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md).\n53\t\n54\t## License\n55\t\n56\t[GPL-3.0](LICENSE)\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"45379bcf-1105-43f4-9d7c-90b4cdbd049a","uuid":"6a637241-1547-4563-a465-ada55fee05dc","timestamp":"2026-11-25T08:50:17.775Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/work/README.md","content":"# ard — automated repository development\n\nard makes a GitHub repository maintain itself. Scanners file deduplicated issues, triage agents turn each issue into a plan, a worker agent implements it on a branch, reviewer agents critique the PR, and a merger lands it once every review passes.\n\n**Documentation:** <https://albertcbrown.github.io/ard/> (sources in [docs/site](docs/site)).\n\n> **Status:** under active development. The design lives in [docs/proposal.md](docs/proposal.md), and the work is tracked as [GitHub issues](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues) grouped into phase milestones.\n\n## How it works\n\nOne rule holds the system together: **a deterministic controller owns every GitHub and git side effect; agents only read and write files in a worktree.**\n\nOne `ard` process per repository runs six loops that share a small pool of job slots (default 3):\n\n| Loop | Every | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Scanners | 4 h | Find problems (CVEs, outdated components, lint, docs, missing tests…), file or update issues, close what is fixed |\n| Triage | 15 min | Role agents (lead, PM, architect, designer, doc planner, engineer) turn an issue into `plan.md` |\n| Workers | 5 min | Implement the plan on `worker/<role>-<issue#>-<slug>`, run tests, open a draft PR |\n| Reviewers | 5 min | Role agents (security, license, eng, PM) review the PR and request fixes |\n| Merger | 5 min | Squash-merge PRs whose reviews all passed and whose checks are green |\n| Reaper | 1 min | Mark dead or overdue jobs `ard:executor:failed`, keep their evidence 24 h |\n\nGitHub labels prefixed `ard:` are the queue and the state machine. `.ard/<issue#>/` in the target repository holds each issue's plan, per-role summaries and full agent logs.\n\n## Configuration by convention\n\nA target repository opts in with an `.ard/` directory. A role exists because its directory exists:\n\n```\n.ard/\n├── config.yaml          # global settings and overrides only\n├── scanners/<name>/     # scan (executable) or prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n├── triage/<name>/       # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n├── workers/<name>/      # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n├── reviewers/<name>/    # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts\n└── <issue#>/            # per-issue output and logs, written only by ard\n```\n\nSee [Configuration](docs/proposal.md#configuration) in the proposal for the full schema and defaults.\n\n## Development\n\nRequires Go (see `go.mod`).\n\n```bash\nmake build   # builds bin/ard\nmake test    # go test ./...\nmake lint    # go vet and a gofmt check\n```\n\nContributor and agent guidance is in [CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md).\n\n## License\n\n[GPL-3.0](LICENSE)\n","numLines":57,"startLine":1,"totalLines":57}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018fn39gKBj6trWmF8WhMwbQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
